---
/**
 * When to use PopSub and when not to, in the README's own terms.
 */
---

<div class="panels not-content">
  <section class="panel good">
    <h3>A good fit</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Small applications that want durable realtime messaging on one machine.</li>
      <li>Browsers, services and workers in different languages on one broker.</li>
      <li>Teams that want delivery guarantees written down precisely.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="panel elsewhere">
    <h3>Look elsewhere</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Replication or high throughput today: NATS JetStream or Kafka.</li>
      <li>Devices that only speak MQTT: Mosquitto or EMQX.</li>
      <li>A stable API: PopSub is 0.x, and the <a href="https://github.com/soumyadepp/popsub/blob/main/docs/DESIGN.md#12-known-gaps-in-priority-order">known gaps</a> are listed in priority order.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .panels {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(18rem, 1fr));
  }
  .panel {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--pop-border);
    border-radius: var(--pop-radius-xl);
    background: var(--pop-panel);
  }
  .elsewhere {
    background: var(--pop-bg);
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    color: var(--pop-ink);
    font-family: var(--pop-font-display);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
    font-weight: 550;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--pop-text);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  li::marker {
    color: var(--pop-faint);
  }
  a {
    color: var(--pop-ink);
    text-decoration-color: var(--pop-border-strong);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
</style>
